# ── Personal layer (never committed) — the "one privacy rule" ───────────
# Personal/business content stays local. NOTE the `dir/*` form (not `dir/`): git never descends
# into a fully-excluded directory, so `!dir/placeholder` can only re-include a file when the
# directory itself is still walked. Same trick as docs/prompts/* below.
context/*
inbox/*
daily/*
notes/*
projects/*
areas/*
resources/*
decisions/*
brain/
# Your personalized dashboard. Forkers start from the template (cp templates/home.md home.md).
# Anchored to the root so the data-free templates/home.md stays tracked.
/home.md

# Archived personal content — anything moved out of the personal layer keeps its privacy.
# cortex-rm.sh writes archives/removed/; /cortex-audit writes dated archives/<name>-YYYY-MM-DD/.
# One folder, one lifecycle: everything in here is personal, so everything in here is ignored.
# The product's own history used to live here too, which is why this block needed six lines and
# two negations to say which half was shareable. That history is the git log and CHANGELOG.md now.
archives/*
!archives/README.md

# Keep folder placeholders + README templates tracked so the vault stays shareable
!context/.gitkeep
!decisions/.gitkeep
!inbox/README.md
!daily/README.md
!notes/README.md
!projects/README.md
!areas/README.md
!resources/README.md

# Optimized prompts (contain real project/client detail) — keep the convention, not the content
docs/prompts/*
!docs/prompts/README.md

# ── Local tool state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
# Local /slash-command copies of the rituals; canonical skills live in skills/
.claude/skills/

node_modules/

# Generated views (contain personal note titles) — regenerate locally, never commit
cortex.html
# The generators that wrote these three are gone, but an old checkout can still have the pages on
# disk, listing the vault's note titles. An audit called the three lines dead and removed them, and
# pages already on disk went untracked in the same commit (#420). The rules stay as the backstop.
brain.html
navigator.html
cortex-graph.html

# A private team-brain clone (references/living-cortex.md). It must never be committed beside
# public code — the doc said this was already ignored, and it was not.
team/

# Backups (auto-created; noise — never commit)
*.bak
context/.backups/

# ── Vendored third-party skill collections (re-fetchable; keep the repo lean) ──
.agents/
.superpowers/


# Understand-Anything generated artifacts (knowledge graph, dashboard, scratch)
.ua/

# Cortex working artifacts in this repo (index/findings are generated; target repos commit .cortex/memory/)
# This also covers .cortex/local-paths, on purpose: it is how an install exempts a local-only folder
# from the absolute-path check (tools/test/no-private-names.test.sh), and upstream must never ship
# one. A clone that wants its CI to see its declaration commits it with `git add -f`.
.cortex/

# A local, never-committed denylist of your own private project names, read by
# tools/test/no-private-names.test.sh. It stays out of git on purpose: a denylist of private names
# has to be published to work, which is the disclosure it exists to prevent.
tools/test/private-names.local

# Scratch patch scripts. Editing a file through a throwaway Node script is a normal move here
# (heredocs mangle backslashes in regexes); committing one is not.
*.tmp.cjs
*.tmp.mjs
*.tmp.md
